The aggregates' declared source, the capture that was never possible, and the
counters a row has to carry -- trn1.2xlarge 2026-09-12.

What changed:
  - memory_read_agg and memory_write_agg declared neuron-profile. A capture
    replays the NEFF and needs a NeuronCore of its own; an aggregate gives
    every core to a worker and each worker holds the one core it can see, so
    no capture inside a worker can ever succeed. They now declare what they
    measure: summed bytes over the longest worker's elapsed_s.
  - memory_read and memory_write attempt a capture only when a core was
    reserved for it. Before, a worker spent a subprocess per candidate NEFF
    to reach "Logical Neuron Core(s) not available" and put it in the row.
  - _provenance records the counters the registry declares, so the Score can
    be recomputed from the row. Eleven workloads' numerators never reached
    one.

